  "title": "Allow to edit posts",
  "content": "<ol type=\"1\"><li>User can edit his post until several houses. I suggest to allow edit post forever. And any other user should have ability to see post history. This is how <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">stackoverflow</a> works. And people really improve their posts.</li></ol><ol start=\"2\" type=\"1\"><li>Also in <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">stackoverflow</a> there is ability to edit posts of others. And random people really improve and update posts. It works like wikipedia. Let’s try the same system here?</li></ol>",
